  "statement": "Model the core classes of a ride-hailing app. A Trip is requested by a Rider and fulfilled by a Driver. Each Trip exclusively owns a RouteSnapshot (destroyed if the Trip is deleted). To support surge pricing, TripService depends on a PricingStrategy interface implemented by StandardPricing and SurgePricing.",
  "deliverables": [
    "Separate strict ownership from loose associations.",
    "Decouple pricing rules behind an interface abstraction."
  ],
  "hints": [
    "RouteSnapshot has no lifecycle outside its Trip -> use Composition.",
    "StandardPricing and SurgePricing implement PricingStrategy -> use Realization.",
    "TripService depends on the PricingStrategy interface rather than concrete pricing classes."
  ],
